# payload/MANIFEST — the installer's source of truth
#
# One entry per line. `#` starts a comment; blank lines are ignored. No
# globs — every installed path is spelled out explicitly so the installer
# never links or copies something this file did not name.
#
# Entry grammar:
#   link-dir  <payload-relative-path>
#     Symlink the whole directory into ~/.claude/<same-path>. Framework
#     content stays live: `git pull` in the repo updates it instantly.
#   link-file <payload-relative-path>
#     Symlink a single file into ~/.claude/<same-path>.
#   copy-if-absent <payload-relative-path> [<dest-relative-to-~/.claude>]
#     Copy the file into ~/.claude only if nothing is already there — never
#     overwrite live/learned state. The optional second column renames the
#     destination (source and dest share a path when omitted).
#
# `mcp-specs/` and `fragments/` carry NO entries here — they are install-time
# inputs that install.sh reads directly out of the repo, not files it places
# under ~/.claude/.
#
# install.sh v2 (P1) is the sole consumer of this file: it walks these lines
# and builds/repairs the symlink + copy-if-absent state on every run.

